source: hh/tests/cli_conformance.rs
expression: "String::from_utf8_lossy(&out.stdout)"
---
Halfhand records AI agent sessions to a local SQLite database and
replays them faithfully. All data stays on your machine;
Halfhand makes zero network calls.

Recorded sessions can contain secrets present in prompts and
outputs — use `hh delete` to remove them.

Usage: hh <COMMAND>

Commands:
  init         Set up Halfhand: create the data directory and a starter config
  run          Record an agent session inside a PTY
  replay       Faithfully play back a recorded session in an interactive TUI
  inspect      Print non-interactive detail about a session
  list         List recorded sessions, newest first
  rename       Name or rename a recorded session
  delete       Delete a session and garbage-collect its blobs
  doctor       Diagnose the recording stack and report pass/fail per check
  gc           Reclaim disk space: prune orphaned blobs and vacuum the database
  stats        Summarize the store: sessions, events, disk usage, largest sessions
  scan         Scan recorded sessions for secrets and report what was found
  redact       Irreversibly redact secrets from a recorded session in place
  export       Export a session as a JSON bundle, a portable `.hh` archive, or a self-contained HTML page
  import       Import a portable session bundle produced by `hh export --bundle`
  search       Search recorded sessions for text matches (FTS5 full-text search)
  completions  Print a shell completion script for `hh`
  help         Print this message or the help of the given subcommand(s)
  mcp-proxy    Advanced: run an MCP server behind a recording stdio proxy

Options:
  -h, --help
          Print help (see a summary with '-h')

  -V, --version
          Print version

Examples:
  hh run -- claude          record a Claude Code session
  hh replay last            replay the most recent session
  hh inspect a1b2c3 --json  print session detail as JSON
  hh list                   list recorded sessions

Docs: https://halfhand.org/docs/
